      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Given the function  $y=3{x}^{\\pi }+5ln⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Give an exact answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{\\pi }+5ln⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\pi {x}^{\\pi -1}+\\frac{5}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(3\\pi {x}^{\\pi -1}+\\frac{5}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =3\\pi \\cdot {1}^{\\pi -1}+\\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =3\\pi +5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
